The lava ruin is an [[Phenomena/Althane/Cycle|anticyclic]] building sunk in the river of lava that crosses the [[Geography/Althane/The Hollow/index|Hollow]] beneath [[Geography/Althane/Oresk/index|Oresk]]. The ruin lies in the flow and carries a passage through it and then up towards the surface, and travelers know it by its entrance alone: a small dark-steel structure on the bank, with a hallway behind it that descends into the lava.

Inside, the dark steel gives way to brass and copper. The floors are polished to a mirror and the walls are paneled over pipes that knock like hammers, and the machinery still runs. A barred gate closes the far side of the entry room, held by an armature, with a sealed and handleless door to either side. Three workers in red suits tend the pipes and take no notice of anyone who walks in; seen through a visor, metal bars stand where a head should be, and a pale growth is threaded along them.

Beyond the gate a corridor runs between walls of lava, with pillars set along it, and working the valves shuts off the flow and opens the way on. The voice that watches the ruin through its cameras and speaks over its loudspeakers calls itself [[People/Althane/Damien|Damien]]. [[Bestiary/Elementals#Igni Sprite|Igni Sprites]] live in the lava and climb out when it is disturbed.

At the center of the ruin stands a copper chamber built around a great gear shaped like the escapement of a grandfather clock. A water wheel under the floor is pushed by the lava and turns the gear. Armatures stand around the room and reach into the flow with grappling hooks, hauling cooling rocks out and letting them fall again. Copper piping runs through the whole structure in four subsystems, carrying steam and a bluish-purple liquid; where a pipe has failed, the flow backs up and the room grows hot. Magic energy packed into one broken pipe pushes any patch straight back off, and the energy has to be knocked loose before the pipe will hold. Almost the whole ruin is built of copper, and nobody has explained why.

The only room the cameras do not reach lies behind a locked door at the back of the gear chamber. Damien is sure that room is where he is. The ruin also holds a crossbow called the Aegisfur, made from a metal called [[Phenomena/Althane/Hepatian|Hepatian]]. What powers the place feels faintly divine, a small echo of the sort of presence that might grow into a god given ages.
